// Platform for the OTA lab. Builds on the STM32F4 Discovery board that ships
// with Renode (platforms/boards/stm32f4_discovery.repl), which in turn pulls in
// platforms/cpus/stm32f4.repl. That file provides everything phase 1 needs:
//
//   cpu        CortexM (cortex-m4) with NVIC
//   flash      0x08000000, 2 MiB mapped (the linker script limits us to 1 MiB)
//   sram       0x20000000, 256 KiB mapped (linker uses 128 KiB)
//   usart2     UART.STM32_UART at 0x40004400, IRQ 38
//   can1       CAN.STMCAN at 0x40006400, IRQs 19..22 (TX, RX0, RX1, SCE)
//   timer2     Timers.STM32_Timer at 0x40000000, IRQ 28, 10 MHz model clock
//   gpioPortD  with the user LED on pin 12 (sysbus.gpioPortD.UserLED)
//
// Keeping our own .repl gives later phases a place to add things such as a
// CCM RAM region or a second flash bank without editing Renode's files.
using "platforms/boards/stm32f4_discovery.repl"

// Core coupled memory, absent from the stock description. The linker script
// reserves .noinit here for data shared with the bootloader across resets.
ccm: Memory.MappedMemory @ sysbus 0x10000000
    size: 0x10000
